# <type>(<scope>): <subject>            # 50 chars max ---------→ |
#
# <body>                                 # wrap at 72 chars -----------→ |
#
# <footer>
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Conventional Commits — https://www.conventionalcommits.org/
#
# type      Required. One of:
#   feat        A new feature (MINOR bump per SemVer)
#   fix         A bug fix (PATCH bump)
#   docs        Documentation-only change
#   style       Formatting only, no behavior change (whitespace, semi-colons)
#   refactor    Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf        Performance improvement
#   test        Adding or correcting tests
#   build       Build system / external dependencies (e.g., pom, package.json)
#   ci          CI configuration and scripts
#   chore       Housekeeping (release, gitignore) — will NOT appear in changelog
#   revert      Reverts a previous commit — body must reference the sha
#
# scope     Optional. The area of the codebase — e.g., (auth), (billing),
#           (deps). Use consistently within the repo. Keep short.
#
# subject   Required. Imperative mood ("add", not "added" or "adds").
#           No period. Lowercase first letter unless a proper noun.
#
# body      Optional. Explain the WHAT and the WHY, not the HOW. The diff
#           already shows the how. Wrap at 72. Blank line separates from
#           subject.
#
# footer    Optional. Breaking changes and issue references:
#             BREAKING CHANGE: <description>          # MAJOR bump
#             Refs: #123, #456
#             Closes: #789
#             Co-Authored-By: Name <email>
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Examples
#
# feat(auth): add MFA enrollment endpoint
#
# Users can now enroll a TOTP device via POST /auth/mfa/enroll.
# Enrollment returns a base32 secret and a provisioning URL for
# QR-code display. Verification happens on the next login.
#
# Refs: #482
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# fix(billing): stop double-charging on Stripe retries
#
# The webhook handler was idempotent on the outer envelope but not on
# the inner payment_intent — retries produced duplicate line items.
# Added a payment_intent-scoped idempotency key.
#
# Closes: #501
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# feat(api)!: rename /users to /accounts
#
# BREAKING CHANGE: The /users endpoint has been renamed to /accounts.
# All request/response shapes are unchanged. Client SDKs bump to v2.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# To activate this template locally:
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
#
# Consider also adding a commit-msg pre-commit hook that enforces
# the convention (see D15 and .pre-commit-config.yaml).
